{"code":"47-2061.00","title":"Construction Laborers","description":"Perform tasks involving physical labor at construction sites. May operate hand and power tools of all types: air hammers, earth tampers, cement mixers, small mechanical hoists, surveying and measuring equipment, and a variety of other equipment and instruments. May clean and prepare sites, dig trenches, set braces to support the sides of excavations, erect scaffolding, and clean up rubble, debris, and other waste materials. May assist other craft workers.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":7,"share":0.5333},"I":{"score":2.68,"share":0.1493},"A":{"score":1.38,"share":0.0338},"S":{"score":1.23,"share":0.0204},"E":{"score":1.35,"share":0.0311},"C":{"score":3.61,"share":0.232}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":11472,"text":"Tend pumps, compressors, or generators to provide power for tools, machinery, or equipment or to heat or move materials, such as asphalt.","core":true,"importance":4.34,"relevance":80.73,"frequency":4.49},{"id":11465,"text":"Lubricate, clean, or repair machinery, equipment, or tools.","core":true,"importance":4.22,"relevance":81.6,"frequency":4.46},{"id":11458,"text":"Signal equipment operators to facilitate alignment, movement, or adjustment of machinery, equipment, or materials.","core":true,"importance":4.21,"relevance":71.91,"frequency":4.7},{"id":11460,"text":"Position, join, align, or seal structural components, such as concrete wall sections or pipes.","core":false,"importance":4.03,"relevance":44.01,"frequency":4.18},{"id":19838,"text":"Perform site activities required of green certified construction practices, such as implementing waste management procedures, identifying materials for reuse, or installing erosion or sedimentation control mechanisms.","core":false,"importance":4.01,"relevance":37.47,"frequency":2.92},{"id":11457,"text":"Control traffic passing near, in, or around work zones.","core":false,"importance":3.95,"relevance":41.98,"frequency":3.79},{"id":11469,"text":"Install sewer, water, or storm drain pipes, using pipe-laying machinery or laser guidance equipment.","core":false,"importance":3.94,"relevance":null,"frequency":4.59},{"id":11468,"text":"Operate or maintain air monitoring or other sampling devices in confined or hazardous environments.","core":false,"importance":3.91,"relevance":49.8,"frequency":3.24},{"id":11456,"text":"Read plans, instructions, or specifications to determine work activities.","core":true,"importance":3.9,"relevance":86.61,"frequency":4.11},{"id":11467,"text":"Smooth or finish freshly poured cement or concrete, using floats, trowels, screeds, or powered cement finishing tools.","core":false,"importance":3.9,"relevance":37.76,"frequency":null},{"id":11461,"text":"Measure, mark, or record openings or distances to layout areas where construction work will be performed.","core":true,"importance":3.88,"relevance":71.11,"frequency":4.64},{"id":11463,"text":"Erect or dismantle scaffolding, shoring, braces, traffic barricades, ramps, or other temporary structures.","core":false,"importance":3.87,"relevance":61.07,"frequency":null},{"id":11455,"text":"Clean or prepare construction sites to eliminate possible hazards.","core":true,"importance":3.86,"relevance":83.45,"frequency":4.22},{"id":11459,"text":"Dig ditches or trenches, backfill excavations, or compact and level earth to grade specifications, using picks, shovels, pneumatic tampers, or rakes.","core":true,"importance":3.86,"relevance":null,"frequency":4.75},{"id":11462,"text":"Load, unload, or identify building materials, machinery, or tools, distributing them to the appropriate locations, according to project plans or specifications.","core":true,"importance":3.82,"relevance":76.65,"frequency":4.1},{"id":11471,"text":"Provide assistance to craft workers, such as carpenters, plasterers, or masons.","core":false,"importance":3.73,"relevance":49.17,"frequency":null},{"id":11482,"text":"Spray materials, such as water, sand, steam, vinyl, paint,